# Line-ending policy for claude-g615.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS: these are Windows driver sources and they live as CRLF in the
# build tree on C:. Without this file git stored them verbatim, so a sync that
# changed ONE line produced a 6,672-line diff - WinMaliDriver.c once showed
# 13,344 changed lines for a single version-banner edit, and WinMaliBo.c showed
# 344 changed lines for no content change at all. That makes review worthless
# for a collaborator.
#
# text=auto  -> git NORMALISES to LF in the repository, so diffs show real changes.
# eol=crlf   -> but CHECKS OUT as CRLF, so the working copy still byte-matches the
#               build tree and sync_g615.sh's `cmp -s` keeps working.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Docs are read on both platforms and have no build-tree counterpart.
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.bin binary
